<title>UK: Elf/Murco UK refinery enters scheduled shutdown.</title>
<headline>Elf/Murco UK refinery enters scheduled shutdown.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Elf's  120,000 barrels per day (bpd) Milford Haven refinery is due to begin a full scheduled shutdown on Wednesday which will last until the first week of April, a source at the company said.</p>
<p>&quot;Some of the units are already down and they are bringing the crude unit down this afternoon,&quot; the source added.</p>
<p>An Elf spokesman earlier confirmed the refinery would shut down for six weeks from the end of February.</p>
<p>Elf U.K. has a 70 percent stake in the refinery, while the remainder is owned by Murphy Oil's Murco Petroleum.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 8167</p>
